# Documentation

Source: `governance/policies/documentation.md`

Document: architecture decisions (ADRs), relevant constraints, external APIs, security decisions,
complex business logic, non-obvious technical decisions, how to build/test/run/release.

Do not document: what the code already says, session narratives, temporary notes, undecided speculation.

- One source of truth per topic; link instead of copying rule text.
- Update docs in the same change that makes them outdated.
- Mark unverified statements `REQUIRES VALIDATION`; never describe intended behaviour as implemented.
- In AI-DOS docs, label status: "Governance Definition" (convention) vs "Actual Automated Orchestration"
  (enforced by tooling) vs "Conceptual". Never claim automation that does not exist.

Procedure: `skills/documentation/SKILL.md`
